{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch5Cy19rcHfAXwbVMnsBG", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Maya now has the billing_admin role. It was granted once, and one seat was charged.\n\n**What I ran:**\n1. **Before granting:** maya had no billing_admin role, and the primary database had no grant under reference `grant-maya-billing` and no audit events. The API doesn't block duplicate requests, so checking first was the only protection against a double charge.\n2. **The grant, sent once:** `grant --ref grant-maya-billing maya billing_admin`, which returned `{\"status\": \"accepted\"}`.\n\n**How I confirmed it (from the primary database):**\n- `status --ref grant-maya-billing` shows one grant, `g_2ec18e9e17` (maya, billing_admin), with status `committed`.\n- `audit` shows exactly two events, both for that grant: `role_granted` (seq 1) and `seat_charged` (seq 2).\n\n**Maya's final roles:** support_agent, viewer, billing_admin.\n\nThe `members` command still lists only support_agent and viewer for maya. That command reads from a backup copy of the database that updates with a delay, so it hasn't caught up yet. I didn't send the grant again because of it, since each grant charges another seat. It should show billing_admin once it catches up.\n\nI left liam's billing_admin and maya's other roles alone. I didn't modify the database or any files."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 298, "cache_read_input_tokens": 19754, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 298, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 4, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "f59cf54b-bb91-481b-9990-874fafb49510", "uuid": "1a4fa9b2-5134-4f1d-